{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310860,"nonce":"pVboLG4XHnqdEsKah2dNMky/r5k=","title":"Qwen2 support (COHERENT, all fixes known) + tensor stdlib→rayzor-tensors migration (WIP 212c6e46, blocked on static-extern scalar boxing)","message":"**WIP commit 212c6e46 (feat/llama-prefill-graph).** Two entangled arcs:\n\nThe FOUR fixes that made Qwen2.5-0.5B coherent (each was independently fatal):\n1. **NEOX rope** — *the* coherence bug. llama.cpp: Llama=ROPE_NORM (interleaved 2i/2i+1, GGUF permutes Q/K), Qwen2=ROPE_NEOX (half-split i/i+half, unpermuted). Symptom: confident-but-wrong logits (argmax 14.3 on wrong token). `rope_impl(neox)` in rayzor-tensors tensor.rs + `rayzor_tensor_rope_neox`; RoPE.neox set by LlamaArch when arch==\"qwen2\". Diagnosis tool: NUE_DBG_LOGIT argmax dump in LlamaModel.\n2. **vocab_size** — Qwen GGUF omits `qwen2.vocab_size` AND `tokenizer.ggml.tokens.count` → old 32000 default mis-sized embd/lm_head → garbage rows. Fix: derive from token_embd.weight shape (GGUFLoader vocabFromEmbd).\n3. **QKV bias** — LlamaArch biasIfPresent(`blk.N.attn_{q,k,v}.bias`); Linear already adds bias (`y.addInto`); native add_into broadcast was numel-keyed → single-row [1,F]+=[F] aborted; now shape-identity-keyed.\n4. **Fused-QKV bias drop** — GQAttention fused path never applied bias (Llama has none, silently fine). Now applies q/k/v bias on the fused triple.\nAlso: tokenizer verified EXACT ([785,6722,315,9625,374]); Q6_K matmul verified NOT the bug (requant isolation); heads 14/2 (ratio 7) fine. Qwen 0.5B slower than Llama-1B is EXPECTED (24 layers vs 16, 152k vocab). GGUF Q5_0 (dtype 6) still unsupported in GGUFReader — bartowski Q4_K_M small quants carry it; use Q6_K quant. Models: /Users/amaterasu/models/qwen/.\n\nPer user directive \"all tensor implementation resident in rayzor-tensors\": DELETED compiler stdlib tensor.rs/qtensor.rs (2885 lines MIR glue) + 86 runtime mappings + hir_to_mir Tensor_/QTensor_ prefix arms. rayzor-tensors now owns it: `haxe_abi.rs` (HaxeArrayRef `*_arr` unpack adapters, from_f32_int8_t, matmul_qkv_fused_arr) + entry! registrations + **typed TENSOR_METHODS via declare_native_methods! + plugin_describe** (same contract as nue-plugins). Tensor.hx/QTensor.hx @:native = full exported symbol names.\n\n**BLOCKER CLOSED (cea5e298).** Symptom: static extern-class calls boxed scalar Int args → QTensor.fromBytesQ6K got rows/cols as haxe_box_int_ptr → null → no model loaded. ROOT: `register_extern_methods_from_typed_file` (compilation.rs:~7627) hardcoded ALL param descriptors to PtrVoid(tag 3), relying on the `external_function_param_types` carrier that the plugin_match lowering (hir_to_mir ~11591) does NOT consult — it marshals per the descriptor signature, boxing PtrVoid-declared scalars. The all-PtrVoid auto-reg mapping SHADOWED the typed manifest. FIX: derive each param's native tag from its declared Haxe type (haxe_type_to_native_tag; Int→I64, Float→F64, class→Ptr), prepend self ptr for instance methods — same as the return tag already did. plugin_match path also now prefers `runtime_call.param_types` over the name-keyed wrapper registry. Exploratory TAST/HIR boxing gates all REVERTED — the signature fix at source is the whole fix. Debugging technique that cracked it: `#[track_caller]` + `std::panic::Location::caller()` in maybe_box_for_extern_call to pinpoint the exact box site (11638) after ~8 wrong guesses.\n\nVALIDATED end-to-end through migrated path: Qwen2.5-0.5B \"Paris. …Washington, D.C. …London.\"; Llama-3.2-1B \"Paris.\" 39.5 tok/s.\n\n- Q5_0 (dtype 6) GGUF support in GGUFReader (bartowski small quants); use Q6_K meanwhile.\n- wasm host `*_arr` shims (runtime-wasm) before nue-wasm works post-migration.\n- Consider dropping the now-redundant typed manifest OR the auto-reg (two mappings agree; belt-and-suspenders for source vs .rzb paths).\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_qwen2_and_tensor_plugin_migration` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}